# B-05 · Entity graph (`.epe`) — card report

**STATUS: deferred**

Date: 2026-10-31, third pass on this card. Card: `GRAB_BACKLOG.md` §8
`#### B-05 · Entity graph (`.epe`)   L · deps: B-04, T-11, T-13, T-14, T-18` — Do: 1. `CPartProp` per
new part; 2. weapon components + `SWeaponPoint`s per T-11; 3. `SVehicleLight` per T-18; 4. interaction
objects per `t9_interaction.json`; 5. root `health`/`invulnerable` per T-14; 6. keep the camera
reference. Out: `Working/Entity/bm_epe_edits.json` + the `.epe` in the build. Done: `ConvertProperty`
round-trips the built `.epe` to identical XML; every weapon point, light and part name resolves;
`.epe` object count = base + planned additions.

All five deps are `done`. The blocker is **not** a missing dep and **not** a broken tool: the `.epe`
round-trips byte-identically, the weapon donor now exists, and 4 of the 6 Do steps have values in a
recorded file. It is that the card's third Done criterion is `base + planned additions`, and the
planned additions are exactly the three sets no recorded file defines: step 1's prop count, step 2's
`T-WP3`/`T-WP4` point objects, and step 3's 6 new lights. No partial `.epe` was written (a graph with
a guessed addition set is worse than none and every later card stages on it).

This pass also **withdraws one claim** from the previous record: the base graph's 6 `CPartProp` are
not "34 props dropped by the §101/§102 repair". They are the deliberate 5-part shipped-mod mirror
(MODLOG §46) plus the test-083 probe prop (§113). See "Correction to the record" below.

